# Keep the build context small and the image clean.
#
# Without this, `COPY backend/ ./` and `COPY webapp/ ./` drag the host's
# node_modules over the ones just installed inside the image (fragile — host
# binaries and a host-generated Prisma client shadow the container's), ship a
# stale webapp/dist that the build stage is meant to produce, and — worst —
# bake any local .env straight into the image layers.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-ssr

# Secrets never belong in an image layer. .env.example is intentionally kept.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local databases — real accounts and customer data.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite

# Build/tooling noise
**/.git
**/*.log
**/.cache
**/.eslintcache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
**/.claude
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
